 re-read; `nestedRepositoryReason` refuses gitlinks (a path may contain any character, a newline included) and untracked directories that hold a planted repository at any depth, and receipt certification runs it before any Git is run inside a submodule; a gitlink or directory whose name is not valid UTF-8 cannot be matched on disk, so it is refused rather than skipped (an ordinary file with such a name is fine) (untracked directories are searched on disk within a budget, ignored directories are skipped, and exceeding the budget refuses) and is used by `statusOf`, `hasChangesAt`, `worktree remove` and the session helpers. The session helpers (`cli/src/git.ts`: status badge, `/commit`) and the checkpoint manager refuse the same worktrees; status, branch and `/commit` also run against the verified directory, checkpoint internals only check. `getGitInfo` reports the refusal instead of "not a repository". The real repository's own signing and filter configuration is the operator's and is not pinned. Open residuals: checkpoint internals and `copy-ignored` check but do not pin; a submodule's own `.git` swapped after `nestedRepositoryReason`; `git worktree remove` without `--force` runs its own `git status` child that re-reads `.git` after the pre-removal verification (`--force` would skip Git's own submodule safety); task-worktree merge, discard and ignored-output paths in `cli/src/worktree.ts` and other Git calls from before this stack still run plain Git. (2) A clean source whose index differs from HEAD refuses the merge (this replaces the earlier unstage-before-squash and `--only` guards). (3) The target checkout's branch is re-read right before the fast-forward. (4) Renamed `unrecordableWorktree`. (5) The test passes the waiver directly. (6) `cleanReply` drops trailer-shaped lines from the body (Git's trailer grammar: `Key: v`, `Key:v`, `Key : v`, `Key #n`, `BREAKING CHANGE`; legitimate prose such as `Note: ...` goes too); a file name with control, C1 or bidi-override characters no longer reaches the deterministic message, and such a model reply is unusable. Refusal messages show control bytes from agent-controlled paths escaped, and a repository-controlled project `.env` is read only as a small regular file (a symlink to one is followed; a FIFO, device or oversized file is skipped with a warning, so it cannot hang the host); Git's own error line and every printed path are shown with control, C1, bidi and line-separator characters escaped. A failing waiver write after the fast-forward is a note, and one shared `parseSubmoduleStatus` handles paths with spaces; `cli/test/worktrunk_trust.test.ts`, `cli/test/worktrunk_sibling_layout.test.ts`, `cli/test/worktrunk_ai_message.test.ts` |
