characters no longer reaches the deterministic message, and such a model reply is unusable. Refusal messages show control bytes from agent-controlled paths escaped, and a repository-controlled project `.env` is read only as a small regular file (a symlink to one is followed; a FIFO, device or oversized file is skipped with a warning, so it cannot hang the host); the refusal messages (worktree helper, session helpers, checkpoint manager) and Git's own error line are shown with control, C1, bidi and line-separator characters escaped (other merge notes print paths through `shownPath`, which only redacts). A failing waiver write after the fast-forward is a note, and one shared `parseSubmoduleStatus` handles paths with spaces; `cli/test/worktrunk_trust.test.ts`, `cli/test/worktrunk_sibling_layout.test.ts`, `cli/test/worktrunk_ai_message.test.ts` |
  +| WP-1316b | Receipt gate for named-worktree merges: `merge` requires a recorded passing verification for the exact state (head, and tree when dirty), written by an agent run whose deliverable-bound verifier (configured or independent, never a discovered generic command) passed in that worktree, or `--no-verify-receipt --reason` (waiver recorded in the registry) | FIXED in the receipt-gate PR; `cli/test/worktrunk_receipt.test.ts`. Running a project verifier from the CLI stays WP-1313's approval model |
   | WP-1316b review (Entire nexus-code/185: `01M720...` edit saved after the receipt check, ledger rows) | An edit saved between the receipt check and `git add -A` was committed and merged on the strength of the receipt | FIXED in PR #447: the staged tree must equal the checked state (and HEAD must be unchanged for a clean source) before anything is committed; `workingState` leaves `.nexus` out as the commit does; `cli/test/worktrunk_receipt.test.ts` |
   | WP-1312b | Optional model-written merge commit message (`merge --ai-message`): configured provider only (egress policy and receipt apply), diff bounded to 20,000 characters and redacted, labelled untrusted data, reply validated and redacted, deterministic fallback on any failure or a 30 s timeout; an explicit `-m` wins | FIXED in the commit-message PR; `cli/test/worktrunk_ai_message.test.ts` (injected completer; no live provider call was made) |
